# QA agent logs and caches — fixtures below are tracked, these are not
qa/logs/
qa/__pycache__/

# Built from backend/ustat_engine by scripts/build_engine_wheel.py on every
# dev start and build. Not committed: a checked-in wheel is a wheel that can go
# stale against the engine it claims to be, which is precisely the mismatch the
# fingerprint check exists to catch. Absent wheel means local compute is simply
# unavailable and everything falls back to the server, which is safe.
frontend/public/pyodide/wheels/

# Built from backend/ustat_engine_r by scripts/build_r_bundle.py on every dev
# start and build, for the same reason as the wheel above: a checked-in bundle
# is a bundle that can go stale against the R sources it claims to be, which is
# precisely the mismatch the fingerprint check exists to catch. (The vendored
# webR entry below also covers this path; it is spelled out here because the
# reasoning is different — that one is third-party bytes we fetched, this one is
# our own generated artifact.)
frontend/public/webr/bundle/

# Fetched from cdn.jsdelivr.net by scripts/vendor_pyodide.py (`npm run
# pyodide:vendor`), not written by hand. It's a large (tens to low hundreds
# of MB) vendored third-party artifact, not source, so it does not belong in
# git history; vendored.json inside this directory records the exact
# version, source URL, and sha256 of every file it fetched so the contents
# can be reproduced or verified without depending on git for it.
frontend/public/pyodide/runtime/

# Fetched from github.com/r-wasm/webr and repo.r-wasm.org by
# scripts/vendor_webr.py (`npm run webr:vendor`), not written by hand. Same
# reasoning as the Pyodide runtime above: ~48 MB of vendored third-party
# artifact, not source, so it does not belong in git history. This covers both
# the runtime (R.wasm and friends) and the self-hosted R package mirror under
# repo/, which exists so `webr::install()` never has to reach repo.r-wasm.org
# and tell a third party which statistical method a clinician just asked for.
# runtime/vendored.json records the version, source URL, and sha256 of every
# file so the contents can be reproduced or verified without git.
frontend/public/webr/

# Throwaway Pyodide parity harness. Not committed: it is a developer page that
# would otherwise be copied into dist/ and served from the production site, and
# it loads Pyodide from a CDN, which the app deliberately does not do. Its
# fixtures live in qa/parity/ and are read by the backend parity tests.
frontend/public/spike/
